pourT -- pour:=, each and color:=contrast (Tony's first draft, 2026-11-22; SEQ 741). A field written down="*" pour:=aRegistry
holds one template row; the laid-out copy has one copy of the row a member of the registry, in order, each marked with its
member. Under a copy each stands for the member: {each} its value, {each.taG} its name, fill:=each paints it,
{aRegistry.each} is that registry's entry of the member's name. color:=contrast is black or white text from the field's own fill.
PourWords is defined with only Grokking searched, so its black and wall are its own and not cOLOr's (a name on the search
list is reopened, not minted).
PT-1  ptColors: 14 rows, cOLOr's order, whatever fits; the names are the members' names.
PT-2  the swatch text is the member's value and its colour is contrast's: white on black, blue and darkBrown, black on the rest.
PT-3  the swatch pixels are the members' own colours (rows 1, 2, 13, 14); below row 14 the page is pageFill, so there is no fifteenth row.
PT-4  PourWords has entries for black and wall only: those two third cells draw, the other twelve draw NOTHING (no tag).
PT-5  ptThree: a registry of three in a field with room for two: three rows; red (#ef2b2d) reads black text by the 17.9% rule.
PT-6  ptPlain, contrast with no pour: a blue fill reads white, a literal #ffffff reads black, no fill takes the text colour in
      effect (red).
PT-7  the refusals, each by name: pour on a plain down; an empty registry; each outside a poured field (a fill and two inserts).
PT-8  a registry not on the search list is refused at define, as any := is, and the row's field is removed.
PT-9  the definition is never written: its ptRows still holds one row and no each.
